.TH JELLYFIN-WAKE-HDD.CONF 5 "September 2026" "jellyfin-wake-hdd" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf \- configuration file for jellyfin-wake-hdd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf
is sourced as a
.BR bash (1)
script by
.BR jellyfin-wake-hdd (8)
on every run, so values must use bash syntax. It is re-read on every run;
no restart is needed after editing it.
.SH DIRECTIVES
.TP
.B JELLYFIN_URL
Base URL of the Jellyfin server. Default:
.IR http://localhost:8096 .
.TP
.B JELLYFIN_API_KEY
API key with access to the Jellyfin
.I /Sessions
endpoint. Create one under Jellyfin's Dashboard -> API Keys. Required;
the service refuses to run without one.
.TP
.B WAKE_PATHS
Bash array of filesystem paths to
.BR stat (1)
in order to wake the underlying drives. One path per drive or enclosure
that needs waking is usually enough, since reading from any file on a
drive wakes the whole physical disk (and, on enclosures that spin up
members together, the whole enclosure). Required; the service refuses to
run if this is empty.
.TP
.B MIN_SESSIONS
Minimum number of connected Jellyfin sessions (idle or playing) required
before drives are woken. Default: 1.
.TP
.B CURL_TIMEOUT
Timeout in seconds for the request to the Jellyfin API. Default: 3.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
JELLYFIN_URL="http://localhost:8096"
JELLYFIN_API_KEY="0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"
WAKE_PATHS=(
    "/mnt/my-first-hdd/TV Shows"
    "/mnt/my-other-hdd/Movies"
)
MIN_SESSIONS=1
CURL_TIMEOUT=3
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jellyfin-wake-hdd (8)
